release-gates-open: these must be done before a release; remove this file in a reviewed pull request once they are.
- LICENSE names the verified copyright holder (MIT is decided; the holder line still says "to be verified").
- Approved Stoda logo/icon added, or a decision to release without one.
- README wording and the first skill reviewed for release.
- Exact release bytes, security and provenance reviewed; public install and update proven from the published repo.
- The guide's read-only promise in a live session: skill tool declarations pre-approve but don't restrict, so check
  (or enforce) that the guide can't run other commands; and decide how to treat clean/smudge filters a repository
  configures, which `git status` can run (Codex review 14, P1).
